        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In practice, the spindle is revolved ninety five times and as the last turn begins, the sleeve is inserted on the stud. The ninety sixth revolution is completed when the reading on the INDICATOR (4) attains the same value as previously recorded. At that point further movement should be stopped.",
